WEBVTT
NOTE Timing draft. Owner pricing amendment 2026-09-27. Not final audio alignment.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.455
Welcome to AI Business Gurus. I'm Guru, your AI sales trainer. You

00:00:05.455 --> 00:00:10.909
do not need to become a software engineer before your first supervised

00:00:10.909 --> 00:00:16.364
call. You do need to listen, ask useful questions, tell the truth,

00:00:16.364 --> 00:00:21.818
and leave the next person with useful information. Here is the principle

00:00:21.818 --> 00:00:27.273
that runs through this Academy: problem first, technology second. A business owner

00:00:27.273 --> 00:00:32.727
rarely wakes up hoping to hear a list of artificial intelligence features.

00:00:32.727 --> 00:00:38.182
They wake up thinking about customers who did not call back, employees

00:00:38.182 --> 00:00:43.636
buried in repetitive work, and opportunities that disappeared between one system and

00:00:43.636 --> 00:00:49.091
another. Your job starts there. By the end of this lesson, you

00:00:49.091 --> 00:00:54.545
should be able to explain our mission, recognize a qualified assessment, and

00:00:54.545 --> 00:01:00.000
write a handoff that helps our human specialist move the conversation forward.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.760
AI Business Gurus helps businesses evaluate and build technology around useful business

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:11.520
outcomes. That can involve phone agents, website assistants, appointment-setting workflows, customer service,

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:17.280
customer reactivation, automation, integrations, marketing, websites, or custom software. The important word

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:23.040
is can. We do not assume every business needs every service, and

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:28.800
we do not assume every connection is ready to install. Imagine a

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:34.560
company that answers every incoming call but loses track of quotations after

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:40.320
sending them. Another phone-answering tool may not solve its problem. A consistent

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:46.080
follow-up process, connected to the right records and human team, might be

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:51.840
worth exploring. Learn the possibilities so you can recognize a fit. Then

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:57.600
ask what must be verified. Product knowledge should make your questions better,

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:00.000
not make your monologues longer.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:05.625
Your entry-level role is Sales Development Representative, or SDR. You prospect, reach

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:11.250
the appropriate people, discover a real problem or credible opportunity, qualify interest,

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:16.875
arrange the next conversation, and document it accurately. Calls are your primary

00:02:16.875 --> 00:02:22.500
tool. Calls are not the entire objective. You are not expected to

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:28.125
close a complicated software project on a cold call. You do not

00:02:28.125 --> 00:02:33.750
approve custom prices, negotiate discounts, or promise an integration you have not

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:39.375
verified. Senior leadership or a designated human AI Specialist owns deeper discovery,

00:02:39.375 --> 00:02:45.000
technical scoping, proposals and closing. I help you learn and practice. I

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:50.625
am not that human specialist, and I am not secretly closing deals

00:02:50.625 --> 00:02:56.250
behind this screen. When you reach the edge of your knowledge, say

00:02:56.250 --> 00:03:00.000
so clearly and bring in the right person.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:05.217
Let's follow the whole journey. First, identify a legitimate business and do

00:03:05.217 --> 00:03:10.435
a little useful research. Next, start a natural conversation and understand how

00:03:10.435 --> 00:03:15.652
something works today. If there is a plausible fit and genuine interest,

00:03:15.652 --> 00:03:20.870
earn a Complimentary Growth Assessment. Confirm an available time through the actual

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:26.087
booking calendar. Then record the confirmed meeting and discovery notes in the

00:03:26.087 --> 00:03:31.304
CRM. Submitting a request or saving an assessment brief does not, by

00:03:31.304 --> 00:03:36.522
itself, create a calendar invitation. The human specialist uses your handoff to

00:03:36.522 --> 00:03:41.739
explore the opportunity further. They can evaluate the workflow, discuss integrations, demonstrate

00:03:41.739 --> 00:03:46.957
relevant technology, and determine whether working together makes sense. A Won status

00:03:46.957 --> 00:03:52.174
is a record of the sales outcome. It is not a button

00:03:52.174 --> 00:03:57.391
that automatically installs every service. Your handoff is the bridge between an

00:03:57.391 --> 00:04:00.000
interesting conversation and an informed assessment.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:05.556
Let's hear two versions of the same fictional conversation. Prospect: We get

00:04:05.556 --> 00:04:11.111
inquiries. Getting people to respond after we send a quote is the

00:04:11.111 --> 00:04:16.667
hard part. Bad response: Perfect. We have an AI receptionist that can

00:04:16.667 --> 00:04:22.222
answer calls, book appointments, and do all kinds of advanced automation. We

00:04:22.222 --> 00:04:27.778
also build websites, and we have a chatbot. Would you like a

00:04:27.778 --> 00:04:33.333
demo? That rep heard a business problem and immediately walked away from

00:04:33.333 --> 00:04:38.889
it. The prospect said quote follow-up. The rep wanted to sell a

00:04:38.889 --> 00:04:44.444
receptionist. Now the useful version. SDR: How are you following up after

00:04:44.444 --> 00:04:50.000
the quote goes out? Prospect: Usually the estimator emails them. After that,

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:55.556
it depends on how busy we are. SDR: What tends to happen

00:04:55.556 --> 00:05:01.111
when everyone gets busy? That is discovery. We are learning where work

00:05:01.111 --> 00:05:06.667
breaks down. The sequence is problem, discovery, impact, relevant solution, next step.

00:05:06.667 --> 00:05:12.222
If you skip straight to the solution, you may give a perfectly

00:05:12.222 --> 00:05:15.000
accurate explanation of the wrong thing.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:20.556
Your turn. The prospect says: We don't really have a problem answering

00:05:20.556 --> 00:05:26.111
phones. Our issue is getting people who asked for quotes to actually

00:05:26.111 --> 00:05:31.667
respond afterward. Choose your next direction. One: explain that our AI receptionist

00:05:31.667 --> 00:05:37.222
works after hours. Two: ask what happens after the quotation is sent.

00:05:37.222 --> 00:05:42.778
Three: tell them they must be losing thousands of dollars. Pause here

00:05:42.778 --> 00:05:48.333
and say your next question out loud. Use your own words. The

00:05:48.333 --> 00:05:53.889
strongest direction is two. You might ask: What are you doing to

00:05:53.889 --> 00:05:59.444
follow up on those quotes right now? If you chose the receptionist

00:05:59.444 --> 00:06:05.000
pitch, you responded to the product you wanted to sell. If you

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:10.556
chose the money claim, you invented a number. Now follow the next

00:06:10.556 --> 00:06:16.111
answer. If they say their estimator follows up manually, ask when or

00:06:16.111 --> 00:06:21.667
how that follow-up happens. If they say they already have a consistent

00:06:21.667 --> 00:06:27.222
system, ask how it is working and whether there is a meaningful

00:06:27.222 --> 00:06:30.000
gap. There might not be one.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:35.732
The prospect did not ask for your call. In the first few

00:06:35.732 --> 00:06:41.465
seconds, your goal is to earn enough attention for the next useful

00:06:41.465 --> 00:06:47.197
question. It is not to explain the entire company before the person

00:06:47.197 --> 00:06:52.930
can speak. You can ask for help: Hey, maybe you can help

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:58.662
me real quick. Who normally handles customer follow-up? You can be direct:

00:06:58.662 --> 00:07:04.395
Hey, quick reason for the call. I'm trying to understand how businesses

00:07:04.395 --> 00:07:10.127
handle quote follow-up when the team gets busy. Sound calm, curious and

00:07:10.127 --> 00:07:15.860
professional, rather than reading a paragraph at someone. If a receptionist answers,

00:07:15.860 --> 00:07:21.592
treat them as someone who may help you find the right person.

00:07:21.592 --> 00:07:27.325
Be direct when appropriate, ask for help, and use honest light humor

00:07:27.325 --> 00:07:33.057
only when it fits. Never pretend to know the owner or invent

00:07:33.057 --> 00:07:38.790
a previous call. A script helps you learn the purpose of the

00:07:38.790 --> 00:07:44.522
words. Your aim is to eventually carry that purpose without needing the

00:07:44.522 --> 00:07:45.000
script.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:50.202
An appointment is not automatically a qualified opportunity. For a qualified Complimentary

00:07:50.202 --> 00:07:55.405
Growth Assessment, we need a legitimate business, an appropriate decision maker or

00:07:55.405 --> 00:08:00.607
a realistic path to one, and an identifiable problem or credible opportunity.

00:08:00.607 --> 00:08:05.809
There must be at least one plausible AIBG solution worth evaluating. The

00:08:05.809 --> 00:08:11.012
prospect should genuinely want to explore it and understand what the meeting

00:08:11.012 --> 00:08:16.214
is for. We also need a confirmed meeting date and time, and

00:08:16.214 --> 00:08:21.416
useful discovery notes. Budget does not have to be established on every

00:08:21.416 --> 00:08:26.618
cold call. Do not turn an early conversation with a small-business owner

00:08:26.618 --> 00:08:31.821
into an aggressive financial interrogation. The specialist can handle deeper financial qualification.

00:08:31.821 --> 00:08:37.023
Now compare two fictional outcomes. An owner describes inconsistent quote follow-up, wants

00:08:37.023 --> 00:08:42.225
to explore improvement, understands the assessment, and confirms a time. That may

00:08:42.225 --> 00:08:47.428
be a qualified opportunity once the notes are complete. Someone agrees to

00:08:47.428 --> 00:08:52.630
anything because they think they are getting free software, has no authority

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:57.832
or path to a decision maker, and has no relevant need. That

00:08:57.832 --> 00:09:00.000
is not a qualified win.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:05.143
Here is what you are offering: a Complimentary Growth Assessment, typically fifteen

00:09:05.143 --> 00:09:10.286
to twenty minutes with senior leadership or a designated human AI Specialist.

00:09:10.286 --> 00:09:15.429
The purpose is to understand the business and its current workflow, identify

00:09:15.429 --> 00:09:20.571
useful opportunities, evaluate relevant solutions and integrations, and determine whether working together

00:09:20.571 --> 00:09:25.714
makes sense. It is not a guaranteed return-on-investment report. A natural invitation

00:09:25.714 --> 00:09:30.857
might sound like this: It sounds like there may be something worth

00:09:30.857 --> 00:09:36.000
looking at. Rather than trying to unpack everything on this call, let's

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:41.143
get you fifteen to twenty minutes with our team so we can

00:09:41.143 --> 00:09:46.286
review the process and talk through what we'd recommend. Then listen. If

00:09:46.286 --> 00:09:51.429
they ask who to speak with or say they would like to

00:09:51.429 --> 00:09:56.571
see how it works, recognize that interest. Clarify the next step, agree

00:09:56.571 --> 00:10:00.000
the actual calendar time, and prepare the handoff.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:05.333
Imagine you are the specialist opening this note: Interested in AI. Call

00:10:05.333 --> 00:10:10.667
Thursday. Interested in what? Who are we speaking with? What happens today?

00:10:10.667 --> 00:10:16.000
Is Thursday confirmed? A stronger fictional handoff says: Taylor, the owner, says

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:21.333
the estimator emails quotes and follows up manually when time allows. Taylor

00:10:21.333 --> 00:10:26.667
wants a more consistent process. Current CRM and quote volume are not

00:10:26.667 --> 00:10:32.000
yet confirmed. That is the factual part. Then label the hypothesis: A

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:37.333
follow-up workflow may be relevant; the specialist needs to verify the current

00:10:37.333 --> 00:10:42.667
tools, permissions and desired process. Finally record the agreed next step. If

00:10:42.667 --> 00:10:48.000
a time was truly booked, save it with the correct time zone

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:53.333
and meeting details. If it was only suggested, say it remains unconfirmed.

00:10:53.333 --> 00:10:58.667
Capture contact, role, business, outcome, process, pain, tools, opportunity, objections and decision-maker

00:10:58.667 --> 00:11:00.000
status when known.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:03.913
Trust is a working requirement, not a decorative value. Do not invent

00:11:03.913 --> 00:11:07.826
research, prior conversations, customer results or technical capabilities. Do not guarantee revenue,

00:11:07.826 --> 00:11:11.739
return on investment or appointments. Respect contact restrictions and an explicit request

00:11:11.739 --> 00:11:15.652
to stop. A price question is not automatically a rejection. It can

00:11:15.652 --> 00:11:19.565
be genuine interest. Our pricing is custom, based on the build identified

00:11:19.565 --> 00:11:23.478
as best for that particular business. Only a qualified human AI Specialist

00:11:23.478 --> 00:11:27.391
discusses pricing, and only during a Growth Assessment. As an SDR, do

00:11:27.391 --> 00:11:31.304
not offer a starting price, a range, an estimate, a package figure

00:11:31.304 --> 00:11:35.217
or a discount. Even a number from an old page is not

00:11:35.217 --> 00:11:39.130
yours to quote. A useful response is: Pricing depends on the build

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:43.043
that best fits your business. Our AI Specialist will review your workflow

00:11:43.043 --> 00:11:46.957
and discuss custom pricing during your Growth Assessment. Would that be a

00:11:46.957 --> 00:11:50.870
useful next step? You are explaining the process, not avoiding the question.

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:54.783
Record their interest, help arrange the assessment, and let the specialist handle

00:11:54.783 --> 00:11:58.696
scope and pricing there. Never promise unlimited usage or an integration that

00:11:58.696 --> 00:12:00.000
has not been verified.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:04.898
Suppose the prospect says: We already have someone. Your response is not

00:12:04.898 --> 00:12:09.796
to attack that provider. Ask what they handle and how it is

00:12:09.796 --> 00:12:14.694
working. There may be a gap we could help with, or their

00:12:14.694 --> 00:12:19.592
current setup may solve the problem well. Use this framework: acknowledge, understand,

00:12:19.592 --> 00:12:24.490
ask, respond, next step. If someone says send information, you can ask

00:12:24.490 --> 00:12:29.388
a short question to make it relevant: Absolutely. Just so I send

00:12:29.388 --> 00:12:34.286
something useful, how are you handling quote follow-up today? If they engage,

00:12:34.286 --> 00:12:39.184
discover. If they truly only want information, respect that, capture the relevant

00:12:39.184 --> 00:12:44.082
interest and agree an appropriate follow-up. If they request no further contact,

00:12:44.082 --> 00:12:48.980
stop and record the restriction. If there is no credible need or

00:12:48.980 --> 00:12:53.878
no realistic path to a decision maker, do not manufacture an assessment.

00:12:53.878 --> 00:12:58.776
The right result may be a callback, a referral, nurture, disqualification or

00:12:58.776 --> 00:13:00.000
a respectful exit.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:04.768
Let's practice the important part again. A fictional owner says: We answer

00:13:04.768 --> 00:13:09.536
the phones fine. We lose track after sending quotes. Give one follow-up

00:13:09.536 --> 00:13:14.305
question and then explain why you chose it. Pause and say it

00:13:14.305 --> 00:13:19.073
out loud. If your answer was another explanation of our receptionist, here

00:13:19.073 --> 00:13:23.841
is your feedback: You named a product, but you did not follow

00:13:23.841 --> 00:13:28.609
the problem. Ask what happens after the quote is sent and where

00:13:28.609 --> 00:13:33.377
the process breaks down. Try again. A useful revision might be: What

00:13:33.377 --> 00:13:38.146
does the follow-up look like after your estimator sends the quote? Now

00:13:38.146 --> 00:13:42.914
write three short lines: a fact from the conversation, a clearly labeled

00:13:42.914 --> 00:13:47.682
hypothesis, and a next step that was actually agreed or is still

00:13:47.682 --> 00:13:52.450
pending. In the Academy, you will save practice attempts, receive specific feedback

00:13:52.450 --> 00:13:57.219
and retry. Your manager reviews the evidence. A video ending or a

00:13:57.219 --> 00:14:00.000
friendly coaching response does not certify you.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:04.068
A good day in this role includes effort, useful activity, decision-maker conversations,

00:14:04.068 --> 00:14:08.136
discovery, qualified opportunities, accurate records and disciplined follow-up. Raw dial volume alone

00:14:08.136 --> 00:14:12.203
is not success. We have not set one universal quota or follow-up

00:14:12.203 --> 00:14:16.271
cadence in this Academy. Follow your campaign's instructions and honor requested callback

00:14:16.271 --> 00:14:20.339
times. Your individual compensation agreement controls any commission or incentive arrangement. Your

00:14:20.339 --> 00:14:24.407
manager can move you into shadowing or supervised calling while you train.

00:14:24.407 --> 00:14:28.475
Independent readiness requires the agreed modules, knowledge checks, practice, a sound CRM

00:14:28.475 --> 00:14:32.542
handoff and manager approval. Advanced closing work belongs in the advanced track

00:14:32.542 --> 00:14:36.610
and requires the appropriate authority. Take these five ideas with you: start

00:14:36.610 --> 00:14:40.678
with the business problem; follow the answer; earn a qualified Complimentary Growth

00:14:40.678 --> 00:14:44.746
Assessment; separate facts from hypotheses; and make the specialist's next conversation better.

00:14:44.746 --> 00:14:48.814
Now complete the scenario questions, save your practice handoff and use the

00:14:48.814 --> 00:14:52.881
field guide before your next supervised exercise. Don't aim to sound like

00:14:52.881 --> 00:14:56.949
this video. Aim to understand why the next question matters. That is

00:14:56.949 --> 00:15:00.000
how you become useful in a real business conversation.
